{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff (2026-11-16 PST). Scheduled run 43815882263 (2026-11-15 22:18 PST, head b4e0d01b649) is NOT green: it failed only on \"external LLM (live bedrock)\". Root cause: every call those 3 tests made got Bedrock 503 ServiceUnavailableException from us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5. The account's Bedrock invocation log shows 45 such errors for role rebar-external-ci-bedrock between 06:19 and 06:27 UTC. This was not a model-behavior regression: the same tests pass 3/3 locally against the same account and model, and all 4 earlier dispatch runs on the 5.5 models passed. The tests reported the outage as verifier misbehavior. That defect is tracked in leady-soldierly-nurseshark (ef38-6d04-e9cd-4403, relates_to this ticket) and fixed in Gerrit 3404, which is awaiting LLM-Review/Verified. The fix does not stop a Bedrock outage from failing the run, so a scheduled run is still needed. REMAINING for this ticket: wait for the next scheduled external-integration.yml run (cron \"0 6 * * 1\", Sunday 2026-11-22 ~22:15 PST). Check it with `gh run list --workflow external-integration.yml --event schedule -L 1 --json databaseId,headSha,conclusion`. Confirm conclusion=success and that `git merge-base --is-ancestor 91182f96362 <headSha>` holds. Then record the run on this ticket, tick the AC boxes with provenance, and close with close_class preexisting from a worktree fast-forwarded to origin/main. If bedrock fails again with 503s, the message will now say \"the provider failed N/3 runs\" and quote the error."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794869337272486871,"uuid":"2bd0ab38-3c46-414b-8acb-2a7b1cbb7a0b"}